WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.040
so adjusted rates.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.340
And then in your mind,

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.900
is HS or MS likely a bigger indication?

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:07.620
Thank you.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.860
Yeah, I mean, I think I don't know

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.720
if I have the details, Sachin,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.240
that we may have to follow up with you

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.340
on our expectations on the phase three study

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.500
of the design in HS.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.040
But I would still say it's all really going to depend

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.680
in terms of your second part of your question,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.240
the overall data profile that we see.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.620
I think clearly if Remy and MS

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.260
proves itself both in relapse rate

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.240
and disability progression to be better

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.940
than the anti-CD20s,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.180
then of course the opportunity here is massive.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.340
I think if it's in line

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.000
or ultimately a little bit worse,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.920
then I think HS could be a similarly sized indication.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.280
And we know the HS market is growing.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.940
We've guided it to be a 5 billion market growing.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.560
Certainly the petition potential

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.700
is there to be much larger.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.860
And it might be that a safe and effective oral option

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.580
would be required.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.420
But I think it's going to be really, really attractive.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.020
So I think it's really going to be dependent

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:05.940
on that MS readout to understand the size

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.540
of the MS opportunity.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.460
But I think it's exciting that we have two shots on goal

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.900
with Remy to add to what's two already very compelling

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.900
indications that we have going forward.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.160
But we'll get back to you on your question on HS.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.560
Next question.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.160
Thank you.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.560
Your next question comes from the line of Richard Foster

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.600
from JPMorgan.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.560
Please go ahead.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.560
Hi.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.440
Thanks for taking my question.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.520
A question about China.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.800
You reference competition for Cosentix,

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.680
but we also saw much lower growth in general in China

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.200
across Q1, despite the strong start for Lecveo.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:49.400
So should we expect more slower international growth

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.320
for Entresto, Cosentix going forward,

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.760
and slower overall China development?

00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:00.760
Or can Lecveo continue to drag China growth to double digits?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:01.320
And I have one question.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.400
I have one quick linked question on Lecveo.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.160
How much of a peak do you think can come from China,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.400
given the strong start?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.240
Thanks very much.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:11.440
Yeah.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.040
Thanks, Richard.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.080
So overall, the dynamics in China,

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.240
we've seen a stabilization in the early part of this year.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.680
I don't think we're back to the pre-2025 growth levels,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.160
but we do see a stabilization overall in the market

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.200
as well and in our key segments.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.080
And so we feel confident that our China business can be in that high, single,

